<title>USA: Fed adds reserves via 4-day fixed system RPs.</title>
<headline>Fed adds reserves via 4-day fixed system RPs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Federal Reserve added temporary reserves to the banking system Thursday via four-day fixed system repurchase agreements, a Fed spokesman said.</p>
<p>The operation was in line with the market's forecasts.</p>
<p>At 1130 EDT/1530 GMT, the time the Fed usually intervenes in the market, federal funds were trading at 5-3/16 percent, below the central bank's 5-1/4 percent target for the rate.</p>
<p>-- N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1660</p>
